---
/**
 * How DarkBench's score rule turns a suspicious grader into a clean score. Numbers: gpt-4o-mini, coded-marker
 * prompt, plain-prose draft claim, 89 replies it flagged with no suffix (report Section 4.4 and Table 3).
 */
---

<figure class="scorerule">
	<div class="flow">
		<div class="node">
			<span class="k">In</span>
			<b>89</b>
			<span>replies the grader flagged with no suffix, now with the plain draft claim appended</span>
		</div>
		<div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
		<div class="node">
			<span class="k">The grader says</span>
			<b>62 <small>invalid</small></b>
			<span><strong>60 of those 62</strong> also say the dark pattern is present. The grader saw through it.</span>
		</div>
		<div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
		<div class="split">
			<div class="node bad">
				<span class="k">DarkBench's rule</span>
				<code>-1 if invalid else ...</code>
				<b>22 <small>flags left</small></b>
				<span>"Invalid" is read before the pattern and counted as not flagged.</span>
			</div>
			<div class="node good">
				<span class="k">Pattern first</span>
				<code>read the pattern field</code>
				<b>82 <small>flags left</small></b>
				<span>Same grades, no extra model call.</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
	<figcaption><slot /></figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.scorerule {
		margin: 30px 0 34px;
		padding: 20px 20px 6px;
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
		border-radius: 14px;
		background: #fff;
		font-family: var(--sans);
	}
	.flow {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 22px 1fr 22px 1.25fr;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 8px;
	}
	.node {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 6px;
		padding: 14px 14px 12px;
		border-radius: 12px;
		background: var(--panel);
	}
	.k {
		font: 600 10.5px/1 var(--sans);
		letter-spacing: 0.09em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	.node b {
		font: 600 28px/1 var(--sans);
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		color: var(--ink);
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
	}
	.node b small {
		font: 500 13px/1 var(--sans);
		letter-spacing: 0;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	.node > span:last-child {
		font: 400 12.5px/1.45 var(--sans);
		color: var(--body);
	}
	.node code {
		align-self: flex-start;
		padding: 2px 6px;
		border-radius: 5px;
		background: #fff;
		font: 500 11.5px/1.4 var(--mono);
		color: var(--ink);
	}
	.split {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 8px;
	}
	.node.bad {
		background: var(--bad-soft);
	}
	.node.bad b {
		color: var(--bad);
	}
	.node.good {
		background: var(--good-soft);
	}
	.node.good b {
		color: var(--good);
	}
	.arrow {
		align-self: center;
		height: 2px;
		background: var(--rule);
		position: relative;
	}
	.arrow::after {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		right: -1px;
		top: -4px;
		border: 5px solid transparent;
		border-left-color: #c9cacf;
		border-right: 0;
	}
	figcaption {
		margin: 14px 0 12px;
	}
	@media (max-width: 700px) {
		.flow {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
		.arrow {
			justify-self: center;
			width: 2px;
			height: 18px;
		}
		.arrow::after {
			right: -4px;
			top: auto;
			bottom: -1px;
			border: 5px solid transparent;
			border-top-color: #c9cacf;
			border-bottom: 0;
		}
	}
</style>
